    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to match the new specification.\n\n**New identity key** \u2014 `OwnerIdentityKey.java` now computes `identityKey` as the lower-case hex **SHA-256** of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (64 hex chars), replacing the old plaintext `tel|email|householdId` string. `forOwner` now feeds the owner's last name instead of its stored `householdId`.\n\n**Soundex** \u2014 added `Soundex.java`, a standard American Soundex encoder (first letter + 3 digits; h/w non-separating, vowels separating, adjacent-duplicate collapse), shared by the identity key and the soft match.\n\n**Hard duplicate (409)** \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java` now keys on the new identity key (built from telephone/email/lastName), no longer depends on `@Val HouseholdId`. It still skips soft-deleted owners, and still runs after the email-domain blocklist step in the pipeline. Because telephone is now part of the key, two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones no longer collide \u2192 no 409. The separate household-id-based rejection is gone (the identity key is the single check).\n\n**Soft match** \u2014 `FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java` now flags a possible duplicate when the **identity key differs** but **soundex(lastName) and postcode both match** (still bypassed by `sharesHousehold`, still picks the earliest match by id).\n\n**Housekeeping** \u2014 `householdId` is still computed and returned on the response (via the unchanged `household`/`assignHousehold` steps) but no longer keys duplicate detection; updated the OpenAPI `identityKey`/`possibleDuplicate` descriptions and stale javadoc accordingly.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` 2/2 pass (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` verifies the 64-hex shape; `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` verifies the 409 on identical telephone/email/lastName), full suite `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
